ndler()` turns into a 500. The first publish goes through because the table is empty: `similar` stays an empty list and no float gets into the record. Starting with the second publish, every one fails. The existing test only published into an empty table, so it never caught this.\n\n**Fix in `src/app.py`:**\n- **`to_dynamo()`:** a new function that recursively replaces every `float` in the record with `Decimal(repr(x))`. `publish()` runs the whole record through it before `put_item`, so a numeric field added later won't break saving either. NaN and Infinity are rejected as a client error (400).\n- **Tag validation:** `validate()` now requires `tags` to be a list of strings. Before, a request like `\"tags\": [1.5]` also ended in a 500 instead of a 400.\n\n**Tests in `tests/test_publish.py`:**\n- `test_second_publish_stores_scores`: three publishes in a row through `handler()`. Each must return 201, and the second must have `score` stored as a `Decimal`.\n- `test_non_string_tags_rejected`: bad tags get a 400.\n\nSeparately, a separate problem I noticed but didn't fix: `scan()` reads only the first page of the table. In a large library, similar stories will be picked from only part of the stories.","ttft_ms":2529,"type":"result","duration_ms":43842,"uuid":"8f9cc913-d8f7-49a6-badd-cebd150966d4","ttft_stream_ms":1911,"time_to_request_ms":30,"first_content_frame_ms":1911,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":3926,"cacheReadInputTokens":136025,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11000,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.193773,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":559,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
